<manifest version="1.0" type="framework">
    <!-- vendor.qti.hardware.qccsyshal@1.1 used to be declared here. It cannot run
         on Android 15: vendor.qti.hardware.qccsyshal@1.1-halimpl.so is built
         against protobuf 3.9-era internals and needs seven symbols the platform
         libprotobuf no longer has, starting with

           CANNOT LINK EXECUTABLE "/system/system_ext/bin/qccsyshal@1.1-service":
             cannot locate symbol "_ZN6google8protobuf8internal14AddDescriptorsE
             PKNS1_15DescriptorTableE"

         (also InitSCCImpl, AssignDescriptors, ArenaImpl::AllocateAlignedAndAdd-
         Cleanup, Arena::OnArenaAllocation and both WireFormat::SerializeUnknown-
         Fields overloads - too much surface to shim the way CBS_init was).

         So the service crashed on every start, and the declaration made clients
         wait for a HAL that was never going to appear - 30 failed lookups in a
         thirty-second sample:

           E init: Could not find 'vendor.qti.hardware.qccsyshal@1.1::IQccsyshal/
                   qccsyshal' for ctl.interface_start

         compatibility_matrix.xml lists it optional="true", so dropping it is
         fine. The service binary and its init rc are no longer installed either;
         the libraries stay in case the protobuf side is ever sorted out. -->
</manifest>
